---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Cookie Policy — PrenupAnswers"
  description="PrenupAnswers cookie policy: what we use (almost nothing), how affiliate cookies work, and how to control your choices."
>
  <section class="article-head">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="crumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / Cookie Policy</p>
      <h1>Cookie policy</h1>
      <p class="meta">Last updated: September 28, 2026</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      Short version: <strong>we run this site with almost no cookies.</strong> No advertising cookies today, no
      cross-site tracking, and our calculator never sends your inputs anywhere. Here is exactly what that means.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies we set ourselves</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>None.</strong> There is no account system, no session cookie, and no personalization cookie on
      prenupanswers.com. Your cookie choice (if you make one in the banner or preferences panel) is stored in your
      browser's local storage under the key <code>pa-consent</code> — it never leaves your device.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      We use <strong>Cloudflare Web Analytics</strong>, which is cookieless: it counts page views, referrers, and
      countries in aggregate without identifying you and without setting a cookie. Because nothing is stored on your
      device, no consent is required for it.
    </p>

    <h2>Affiliate cookies</h2>
    <p>
      When you click a link to a partner (currently HelloPrenup and First), the
      <strong>partner's site</strong> may set a cookie after the click to credit the referral if you later purchase.
      Typical duration is 60 days. These cookies belong to the partner, are governed by the partner's own policy,
      and cost you nothing — commissions come out of our payout, not your price.
    </p>
    <p>
      Prefer no tracking? Open links in a private/incognito window, or clear your cookies after visiting — every
      purchase works the same way either way.
    </p>

    <h2>Advertising (not active yet)</h2>
    <p>
      This site is not currently running display advertising. If we add ad partners (Google AdSense or a
      mediavine-style network), advertising cookies will be set <strong>only after you accept them</strong> in the
      consent banner, and this page will be updated before that happens.
    </p>

    <h2 id="manage">Your choices</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="#manage" data-open-cookie-prefs>Open cookie preferences</a> — view or change your choice at any time.</li>
      <li>Most browsers let you block or delete cookies entirely in Settings → Privacy.</li>
      <li>Questions or data requests: <a href="mailto:hello@prenupanswers.com">hello@prenupanswers.com</a> (also your channel for CCPA, GDPR, and LGPD rights under our <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>).</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>We'll update this page — and the date above — before any new cookie category goes live.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
